  <iati-identifier>CH-FDJP-110.162.567-FIND2021</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="CH-FDJP-110.162.567" type="30">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Foundation for Innovative New Diagnostics</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensure equitable access to reliable diagnosis around the world</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite  the  ongoing  challenges  of  the  COVID-19  pandemic,  FIND  capitalized  on  its recently launched strategy and achieved its 2021 goals, delivering an average of 81% of  programmatic  performance  objectives  (versus  80%  target).  Outside  COVID,  four products  in  FIND&#x2019;s  product  development  portfolio  received  regulatory  clearance; evidence   was   generated   to   support six World   Health   Organization   (WHO) recommendations and policy documents; and 36 clinical studies were conducted, 28 of which relied on newly developed approaches to remote work and remote training. Notably, in 2021, FIND was especially focused on its role in supporting global access to COVID-19 tests and genomic sequencing, through its role in the Access to COVID-19  Tools  Accelerator Diagnostics  Pillar  (ACT-A  Dx).  In  part,  this  meant  engaging substantially with multiple global agencies, and absorbing a large injection of COVID-19 work into ongoing work across FIND&#x2019;s disease portfolio, including in pandemics threats.</narrative>
  </description>
